/-!
# MassGap.GaugeE8 — compact `E₈` as a `GaugeGroup`

The smallest representation of `E₈` is the adjoint, of dimension `248`. `E₈` here is the subgroup
of `SO(248)` preserving the Lie bracket of compact `e₈`, written in an orthonormal basis.

## The bracket

`research/code/e8_structure.py` builds compact `e₈` from the root lattice (Kac, *Infinite-dimensional
Lie algebras*, §7.8): Bourbaki simple roots in standard coordinates of `ℝ⁸`, the bimultiplicative
cocycle `ε(α, β) = (−1)^(Σ aᵢbᵢ + Σ_{i<j} aᵢbⱼ(αᵢ, αⱼ))`, and the complex algebra
`[Hₖ, e_α] = αₖ e_α`, `[e_α, e_{−α}] = −Σ αₖ Hₖ`, `[e_α, e_β] = ε(α, β) e_{α+β}`. The real basis,
indexed by `Fin 248`, is

* `0, …, 7`: `i H'ₘ` with `H'_{2s} = H_{2s} + H_{2s+1}`, `H'_{2s+1} = H_{2s} − H_{2s+1}`;
* `8 + 2r`, `9 + 2r`: `e_α + e_{−α}` and `i (e_α − e_{−α})` for the `r`-th of the `120` pairs
  `{α, −α}`, the representative chosen with `λ(α) = α₁ + α₂ ≥ 0` and the pairs ordered by `λ`
  descending (`λ = 2` once, `λ = 1` for `r = 1, …, 56`, `λ = 0` for `r = 57, …, 119`).

In this basis the structure constants `f_{ijk} = ⟨[xᵢ, xⱼ], xₖ⟩` are integers in `{±1, ±2}` and
totally antisymmetric, and the Killing form is `−120 · 1`. They enter Lean as the 3-form
`phiE8 = Σ_{i<j<k} f_{ijk} eⁱʲᵏ` (`e8Blocks`, 4936 triples), and the bracket is
`br x y m = phiE8 x y eₘ`, so `[xᵢ, xⱼ] = Σₖ f_{ijk} xₖ`. The generator checks, in floating point
on the integer data and in under ten seconds: total antisymmetry, the Jacobi identity coefficient
by coefficient, `tr(ad xᵢ ad xⱼ) = −120 δᵢⱼ`, and that a single flipped sign breaks Jacobi. None of
this is re-proved in Lean: Lean does not prove that `br` satisfies the Jacobi identity, that it is
simple, or that it is `e₈`. What Lean carries is the definition from the data and the one
derivation `cartanM` below, checked against the data by the kernel.

## Objects

* `E8Sub`: `{g ∈ SO(248) | ∀ x y, g [x, y] = [g x, g y]}`; `E8` is its carrier type.
  Mathematically this is `Aut(e₈) ∩ SO(248)`. For the compact form, `Aut(e₈)` is the adjoint group
  (no outer automorphisms, trivial centre), compact and connected, so it lies in `SO(248)` already
  once it lies in `O(248)`, which it does because automorphisms preserve the Killing form. None of
  that is used or proved here; the intersection with `SO(248)` is part of the definition.
* `isClosed_E8Sub`: closed in `SO(248)`, an intersection of zero sets of continuous maps; `E8` is
  compact as a closed subset of the compact `SO(248)`.
* `e8Rep`: `SO(248)`'s `soRep 248` restricted to `E8Sub` — the adjoint representation.

## Instances

* `instGaugeGroupE8`: compact, second-countable, Borel, with `e8Rep` faithful and continuous.
* `instGaugeSimpleE8`: `lieDim = 248`, `dualCoxeter = 30`, `dynkinIndex = 30`. Classification
  values, entered as constants like every other `GaugeSimple` instance; nothing here derives them
  from `E8Sub`. The normalisation of `GaugeSimple` (long roots of squared length two) has
  `T(adj) = h^∨`: at `SU(N)` the adjoint has `T = N = h^∨` against `T(fund) = 1/2`, at `SO(n)`,
  `n ≥ 5`, `T(adj) = n − 2 = h^∨` against `T(vector) = 1`. The representation here is the
  adjoint, so `T = h^∨(E₈) = 30`.
* `instGaugeLieE8`: `lieGen X` is `X` Hermitian, `Xᵀ = −X`, and `X` a derivation of the bracket
  over `ℂ`, `X [x, y] = [X x, y] + [x, X y]`. A Hermitian antisymmetric `X` is `i B` with `B` real
  antisymmetric, and the derivation condition on `X` is the same condition on `B`. That the real
  span of `lieGen` has dimension `248` is not proved here.

## The generator `cartanM`

`cartanM = i · ad(x₀)`, `x₀ = i H'₀`: it rotates each pair `(x_{8+2r}, x_{9+2r})` by `λ_r` and
kills the Cartan directions, `(cartanM v)ₙ = i dN n · v (pN n)`. `lieGen_cartanM` proves it
Hermitian, antisymmetric, a derivation of `br`, and nonzero. The derivation property is proved as
invariance of the 3-form: `cartanM` acting on `phiE8` is, triple by triple, a sum of `eⁱʲᵏ` with
integer coefficients, and `e8Blocks_ok` checks by kernel reduction (`decide +kernel`, no
`native_decide`) that within each block of `e8Blocks` the coefficients of every non-degenerate
index triple cancel. Blocks are the triples sharing a slot triple (slot of `n < 8` is `n`, of
`8 + 2r` and `9 + 2r` is `8 + r`); `cartanM` preserves slots, so cancellation within blocks is
the whole condition.

## The Clay statement at `E₈`

`ClayStatementE8 := ClayStatementOf E8`. `ObserverLinkedG.clayStatementAtG_of_observer (G := E8)`
elaborates, concluding `ClayStatementAtG E8 W (SymPlaqClassG E8)` from its inputs, and
`clayStatementE8_of_atG` with `SymPlaqG.symPlaqG_refl E8` turns that into
`ClayStatementOfDy E8`, the statement at the frozen tower;
`MeasuredSpacing.clayStatementMeasOf_of_of` lifts it to
`ClayStatementE8` under asymptotic scaling of the tensor mass.
-/

